Hand pi a call to one of its own tools that isn't loaded, and say what
broke a relayed stream.

A model that reaches for a pi tool it has only read about (one loaded on
demand, such as jobs) started a tool call pi's translator refused by
throwing. The relay caught it and kept only the error's class, so the turn
ended as "relay failure Error" and Claude Code's retry was denied: every
turn the model reached for the tool, with nothing naming it. Every other
provider hands such a call to pi, which answers "Tool jobs not found" and
the model goes on. So a call in pi's namespace goes to pi whether or not
the tool is active, a tool outside it still ends the turn, and a relay
failure carries its message.

